{
    "background_story": "Imani was a free-spirited artist who lived life on her own terms. Growing up, her parents had always been overprotective, coddling her to the point where she felt suffocated. They meant well, but their constant hovering and criticism stifled her creativity and independence. As soon as Imani left for college, she reveled in the freedom to make her own decisions and take risks. She began to explore her passion for painting, experimenting with bold colors and techniques. However, when her parents visited her on campus, old habits resurfaced, and they began to offer unsolicited advice on her art. Imani had to gently remind them that she was capable of navigating her own path, and that their coddling, though well-intentioned, was holding her back from truly flourishing.",
